scopecontent><p> Baron de Berlepsch [to Marlborough]: his secret meeting with Sieur Reichart has taken place, and resulted in the enclosed list [<extref href=&#34http://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/SearchUI/details?Uri=C8950282&#34>SP 87/2/42</extref>] of demands by the elector of Bavaria. Reichart showed him a letter from Tallard to the elector: Tallard's army was 35,000 strong, and he had promised the elector assistance with money, provisions and munitions. [Reichart said that] the duke of Savoy was ready to treat with France. Reversals for the allies in Spain, Italy and Hungary. Prince Louis of Baden had made approaches to the elector through a third party, and Prince Eugene was authorized to do so. [Berlepsch] is returning to Berlin, and from thence to Vienna, after which he hopes to visit Marlborough. Dated at Nuremberg. On dorse, copy of a letter [to Berlepsch] at camp at Ober Aching: he welcomes him and requests him to remain hidden. He has found a pretext to meet him in four or five days. ff. 75-78</p></scopecontent>","ephemera":null,"schema":null},"digitised":false,"heldBy":[{"xReferenceId":"A13530124","xReferenceCode":"66","xReferenceName":"The National Archives, Kew","xReferenceType":null,"xReferenceURL":null,"xReferenceDescription":null,"xReferenceSortWord":null}],"id":"C8950281","isParent":false,"catalogueLevel":7,"parentId":"C3116440","recordOpeningDate":null,"referencePart":"41","referenceParentId":null,"sortKey":"07 0 441000 0#41000","source":null,"title":null}